diagnosis_text:
Affected component: DNS service (BIND/named) on dns_server with incorrect recursion policy and missing upstream resolution path. Mechanism: Clients resolve internal names (web0.local, etc.) quickly because the server is authoritative for zone “local,” but any lookup outside that zone is refused. Many apps/pages try to fetch external resources (CDNs, telemetry, favicons), so DNS failures manifest as pages “spinning” until timeouts/caches change, then seeming to recover. Localization: On dns_server, named is running and listening (netstat shows 10.200.0.2:53). Host resolvers point only to 10.200.0.2 (/etc/resolv.conf). A query from host_1_1_1_1 returns REFUSED for google.com (dig/nslookup). The BIND config explicit
